        ]
      ],
      "assessment": "Complete body read. Vec<Q> subtraction truncates through zip and has no intrinsic dimension fence; shape fingerprint intentionally excludes coefficients and therefore is not full complex identity. Image membership errors become false, explicitly documented as an inconclusive result rather than an obstruction. The accompanying statement that a uniformly false relation is an equivalence is mathematically false on a nonempty carrier. The external HoTT finite carrier validator does reject failed reflexivity, so this prose defect and direct Vec interface gap do not show a validated quotient bypass. Tests cover an exact two-coordinate path complex, orientation and a finite three-element quotient; they do not check mismatched Vec lengths. Generic capacity records are independent of cohomological semantics. No external solver or Rust execution.",
      "chunk_assessments": [
        {
          "path": "code/rust/core_homology/src/cochain_primitive_difference.rs",
