      "assessment": "Complete body read. Canonical SHA sorts nested object keys and preserves array order, but the hardcoded test fixture differs from the independently computed digest of the exact stated canonical bytes. Constructor checks demand IDs, matrix shapes, nonzero coefficients and coordinate order, but exact d1*d0 and matrix/vector helpers use unchecked i64 arithmetic. Public fields and Serde permit bypassing construction; realization construction does not revalidate an already supplied window. Parameter and closure vectors are zipped without length validation, so missing and extra parameters can produce an exact-repair witness. Nonzero coefficients and matching IDs are coordinate admission, not proof that a presentation is faithfully represented. Tests exercise canonical JSON but omit integer overflow, wrong vector dimensions and malformed deserialized windows. No Rust or serialization execution.",
