      "assessment": "Complete body read. Constructors validate finite nonnegative distortions, bounded xi and matching raw projection lengths; xi itself and harmonic status are caller inputs. Diagnostic edge-count validation checks only projection length, not distortion length or ranking completeness, and witness validation accepts duplicate/arbitrary in-range worst-edge indices. State trait default validates endpoints and finite edge values but implementors remain responsible. Correction silently skips invalid targets and returns unchanged data for invalid strategy; finite convex endpoints can overflow in the subtraction formula and output is not checked. Tests meaningfully cover ordinary sorting, tolerance, NaN, xi, length and small corrections, not these binding/overflow gaps. External numerical functional owners were not executed.",
