      "assessment": "Complete body read. Automatic BFS uses edge identity, extends vertex set from endpoints, handles disconnected components and multiedges, and correctly counts chords as E-V+c for its constructed forest. Potentials are unchecked i64 sums/differences rather than arbitrary exact integers. Designated-tree variant does not validate spanning-forest membership or acyclicity, computes components of supplied tree, and removes edges by endpoint pair rather than edge identity/weight, so certificate.valid checks only a self-consistency count. K4 tests exercise ordinary examples and expected potentials; capacity tests concern independent count wrapper. No independent certificate verifier, explicit cycle coefficient vectors or safe arithmetic guarantee is supplied.",
