          "assessment": "Complete body read. Graph-only projector computes I-B B+ using fixed 1e-10 pseudoinverse cutoff and symmetry averaging; this assumes no 2-cell closure differential and gives no checked idempotence/error bound. Harmonic basis keeps only singular values exactly equal to zero and explicitly discards missing tail values, which cannot recover full nullity when edge dimension exceeds listed singular values. Its orthogonality test multiplies B rather than B-transpose and only loops over returned basis; both tests lack a required nullity cardinality and can pass empty. K5 dimension bound proves missing completeness without executing nalgebra. Generic L4 capacity admission is unrelated to the numerical algorithm."
