          "assessment": "Complete body read. Private group/residue fields enforce modulus>=2 and range; u128 intermediates protect supported 64-bit usize modular addition/difference. Public cochain residues are revalidated at coboundary checking, including length and modulus, with 4096/65536 carrier policy. Component propagation uses both directed edge signs, and positive witnesses are replayed against every edge; nonzero inconsistent residue is an obstruction but lacks an explicit cycle path certificate. Cochain is ordered-coordinate data rather than graph-hash-bound identity. Graph endpoint validity is inherited from FiniteDirectedGraph, whose deserialization issue was separately recorded. Tests cover full-word modulus, mutation, replay and nontrivial holonomy. Discrete group and support-size shell explicitly do not construct continuous U1 or physical phase."
        }
      ]
    },
