      "full_source_read": true,
      "empty_file_read": false,
      "reviewed_lines": [
        [
          1,
          567
        ]
      ],
      "assessment": "Complete body read. Private sparse columns canonicalize duplicates with checked i64 sums, and composition uses checked i128 products/sums and checked narrowing; complex verifies map counts/shapes and all consecutive products. Exact integral homology free-rank and torsion formula is valid because ker(d) is saturated in the free chain group, so adjoining free ambient complement does not alter torsion of incoming-image quotient. SNF and GF2 computations are external, unexecuted dependencies. Dense conversion multiplies unrestricted declared row count by stored column count unchecked and allocates before backend validation. Mod2 Bockstein correctly computes lift/coboundary/halve/reduce for admitted cocycles, but it does not detect all2-primary torsion (d=4 example is zero). Degree and parity checks are explicit; checked integer refusal may conservatively reject large intermediate sums even if final values cancel. Generic capacity test does not bound actual complex allocations or validate SNF.",
      "chunk_assessments": [
        {
          "path": "code/rust/core_homology/src/integral_chain_complex.rs",
          "sha256": "fa3899b50ee9a15f90e85ae11f9663392cd91525f376fdd5740e27931b56be52",
          "lines": [
            1,
            567
          ],
          "empty_file_read": false,
          "assessment": "Complete body read. Private sparse columns canonicalize duplicates with checked i64 sums, and composition uses checked i128 products/sums and checked narrowing; complex verifies map counts/shapes and all consecutive products. Exact integral homology free-rank and torsion formula is valid because ker(d) is saturated in the free chain group, so adjoining free ambient complement does not alter torsion of incoming-image quotient. SNF and GF2 computations are external, unexecuted dependencies. Dense conversion multiplies unrestricted declared row count by stored column count unchecked and allocates before backend validation. Mod2 Bockstein correctly computes lift/coboundary/halve/reduce for admitted cocycles, but it does not detect all2-primary torsion (d=4 example is zero). Degree and parity checks are explicit; checked integer refusal may conservatively reject large intermediate sums even if final values cancel. Generic capacity test does not bound actual complex allocations or validate SNF."
        }
      ]
    },
