      "assessment": "Complete body read. Validates unique strictly sorted vertex lists and a vertex occurrence, then deletes/reinserts the vertex to establish a bijection between the supplied cofaces and generated faces. It never checks input downward closure or that generated faces belong to the original family, so the finite-complex premise is caller-supplied. Star means cofaces containing the vertex, not the full closed star. For an actual simplicial complex the local bijection is correct; a lone edge also passes despite missing faces. The edge example tests only the valid convention.",
