      "assessment": "Read complete range. Constructors enforce nonempty distinct ordered vertices, canonical orientation parity, full face closure and deterministic basis/index maps. Signed boundary and transpose coboundary formulas are mathematically correct on those admitted inputs. Derived Deserialize bypasses all these private-field invariants for Simplex, OrientedSimplex and SimplicialComplex; malformed empty/simplex/index data can reach arithmetic or incorrect matrices. A valid singleton vertex label usize::MAX also overflows ambient max-label+1. Face closure has exponential output and no operative budget. Boundary composition is checked exactly through the external matrix backend. Read complete range. Rational Betti formula checks rank subtraction rather than clamping, relying on constructor-generated simplicial boundaries. Empty convention is storage dimension zero. Vertex/orientation validators reject duplicates, meaningful tests cover circle/disk/sphere, orientation, signed matrices and boundary/coboundary laws through dimension five. These are substantial tests distinct from generic count-capacity controls. They do not cover malformed deserialization, maximum labels or exponential allocation. No Rust or rational backend execution here.",
